{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And I took. A large sheet.</b> Some say from ממגלה, and the yod is in place of a dagesh, like דליו שוקים (Proverbs 26:7)." "<b>With a stylus.</b> Like ויצר אותו בחרט (Exodus 32:4), a cast figure in the shape of a man. Others say that גליון is a singular of גליונים, and it is a garment and the writing is the work of embroidery, and the meaning is that he prophesies concerning the future exile of Samaria."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:42.968447818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}